      "description": "Broadcast-Quality Audio. Absolute Noise Rejection. Road-Ready Durability.\nCapture every vocal nuance and acoustic detail with the Arowana Audioglyph AudioFlux Series microphone cable. Designed for recording studios, broadcast applications, and demanding live stages, this cable ensures your mic\u2019s signal remains pristine from capsule to console.\nEngineered with 99.99% Oxygen-Free Copper (OFC) and our signature advanced dual-shielding, it provides exceptional common-mode noise rejection. Paired with heavy-grade, custom-faceted metal XLR connectors that rival the industry's highest-end standards, this cable delivers uncompromised reliability backed by a comprehensive 2-year warranty.\nKey Features & Benefits 99.99% Pure OFC Core: Ensures highly transparent, uncolored audio transmission, perfect for capturing the delicate high frequencies of condenser mics and the dynamic punch of dynamic mics.\nAdvanced Dual-Shielding Architecture: Utilizes a dense copper shield alongside an aluminum-foil barrier and internal cloth wrap to block out electromagnetic interference (EMI), radio frequencies (RFI), and stage hum. Audiophile-Grade XLR Connectors: Features high-grade metal XLR housings with a unique faceted design for superior grip. The precision-machined, gold-plated pins ensure maximum conductivity and corrosion resistance.Secure Latching Mechanism: The female XLR connector features a rugged, heavy-duty latch to ensure a rock-solid mechanical connection to your microphones, preventing accidental stage disconnects.\n2-Year Manufacturer Warranty: Built for the rigors of touring and daily studio use, every Audioglyph XLR cable is guaranteed against manufacturing defects for two full years.\nTechnical Specifications\nParameter Specification Brand Series Arowana Audioglyph AudioFluxConductor Material 99.99% High-Purity Oxygen-Free Copper (OFC) Shielding Dual Shield (Aluminum Foil with Cloth + Copper)\nConnector Type Premium 3-Pin XLR Male to XLR FemaleConnector\nBuild Heavy-Duty Faceted Metal Shell with Gold-Plated PinsLengths\nAvailable3m (10 ft) | 5m (16.4 ft) | 10m (33 ft)\nWarranty 2-Year Manufacturer WarrantyThe Balanced Audio Advantage\nMicrophone signals are incredibly low-voltage, making them highly susceptible to external noise. The AudioFlux Series leverages a true balanced architecture combined with extreme dual-shielding to ensure that interference is canceled out before it ever reaches your preamp. The durable, highly flexible matte PVC jacket lays flat on stage and coils effortlessly, preventing kinks and internal wire stress over years of heavy use.",
