      "description": "Stage Emergency or your normal pedalboard, power your pedals with a mobile charging power bank or a mobile charger using the \u2018Battery Jack\u2019\nAbsolutely silent as the pedals are technically running on a battery and if you are fan of \u2018battery tone\u2019 you will love this as your main power supply\n5 outs 9V center negative and the output is proportional to the the input source with the maximum limit of 5 amperes.\nCan comfortably power analog & digital pedals along with digital amp sims/processors which run on 9v center negative inputs\nCustom USB cable with 5.5 2.2 mm input jack and integrated on off switch to connect the unit to your power bank and for easy wiring of the board (power cables not included)\nSuper sleek size to save precious real estate on a pedalboard and for easy bypass if you are using it in a Plan B situation when your main power supply fails or gets too noisy in a live situation\nRated for a full 3-4 hour set with a 10000 mah power bank with analog pedals. The run time changes based on the pedal draw and usage of the pedals. You can conserve power by using the integrated on/off switch when the board is not in use\nAbsolutely silent as the pedals are technically running on a battery and if you are fan of \u2018battery tone\u2019 you will love this as your main power supply\n5 outs 9V center negative and the output is proportional to the the input source with the maximum limit of 5 amperes. With normal powerbanks/mobile chargers, expect an output of 1-1.5 amps only which is enough to run 5 analog & digital pedals for around 4hrs\nCan comfortably power analog & digital pedals along with low power digital amp sims/processors which run on 9v center negative inputs\nIMPORTANT: Output of the battery jack is directly proportional to input/capacity of the power bank. Only use high quality power banks with 5V high output features or 20 watt+ mobile chargers",
