      "sku": "AK-DSM-HUMBOLDT-SIMPLIFIER-MKII-PEDAL-MUG343F2",
      "description": "SIMPLIFIER MK-II The State-Of-The-Art on Analog Amp simulation\n\nThe Simplifier MK-II takes the analog amp simulation to a new stage of realism. Much more options, while keeping the instant touch and dynamics that only an all analog device can manage. All...in the same ultra compact footprint.\n\nA continuous quest\n\nShortly after we unveiled the Simplifier Classic in September 2019, several other brands came up with very similar products; Nevertheless, the Simplifier sound held strongly, earning an amazing recognition great sales, reviews and powerful end users experiences. So, what made us stand out from the rest? As our CTO Daniel Schwartz once said: We took the right choices.\n\nWHAT'S NEW? Pre-Amps to the limit\n\nCompletely redesigned preamps with wider gain options\n\nWhat\u2019s new? The Power Amp\n\nA new Dedicated power amp drive allows you to dial the perfect amount of power amp compression for that sweet- spot that only a tube amp can achieve. This controls sets a new level of realism engineered only by DSM Humboldt.\n\nWhat\u2019s new? The Master section\n\nMASTER VOLUME allows you to set any amount of pre and power amp drive at any volume level, avoiding unwanted FX-LOOP distortion.\n\nWhat\u2019s new? Stereo Cabsim\n\nAfter a comprehensive research based on hundreds of response curves from the most renown speakers in the market, we completely redesigned the Cabsim section, replacing the MIC position control for a more useful yet intuitive three profile speakers control\n\nAnything else? Yes! A Built-In Reverb please!\n\nAccording to many users, one of the most desired features on the OG Simplifier was a built in reverb, or at least a room control.\u2028 This is why, we heard this call by loading our new Simplifier, with a side- chained digital PLATE reverb.",
