      "sku": "FOCAL-SHAPE-40",
      "description": '\n      <p>The <strong>Focal Shape 40</strong> is the most compact studio monitor in the Focal Professional line, and the perfect solution for nearfield monitoring. These monitors can be used from 23\u2033 away (60cm), and they have an astonishingly extended low end frequency response. Whether you have a room of less than 107 ft\xB2 (10 m\xB2), or an installation where compactness is paramount, Shape 40 is the ultimate acoustic solution.</p>\n\n      <p>Handcrafted in France, Shape 40 integrates five major acoustic innovations to maximise acoustic transparency, wide stereo imaging, and articulated bass register without masking effects.</p>\n\n      <h3>Flax Sandwich Cone & TMD Surround</h3>\n      <p>The 4-inch woofer features Focal\u2019s patented <strong>Flax sandwich cone</strong> composed of high-quality French flax fibers encased in two thin glass-fiber layers, delivering high rigidity, lightness, and internal damping. Combined with <strong>TMD (Tuned Mass Damper) surround</strong>, it produces a linear response between 1 and 2 kHz while dramatically reducing mid-range harmonic distortion.</p>\n\n      <h3>"M"-Shaped Inverted Dome Tweeter</h3>\n      <p>Focal\u2019s 1-inch aluminium-magnesium inverted dome tweeter features a distinctive <strong>\u201CM\u201D profile</strong> and a Poron\xAE suspension. This design achieves very low directivity for flexible listening positions, silky-smooth transients, and exceptional definition up to 35 kHz without ear fatigue.</p>\n\n      <h3>Dual Side-Firing Passive Radiators (Portless Design)</h3>\n      <p>Engineered without traditional bass reflex ports, Shape 40 utilizes <strong>dual 4-inch side-firing passive radiators</strong>. This allows the monitors to be positioned directly against back walls or in cramped control rooms without boundary bass buildup or port wind noise.</p>\n\n      <h3>Neutral Inductance Circuit (N.I.C.) & Class-AB Amplification</h3>\n      <p>Focal\u2019s proprietary <strong>N.I.C. technology</strong> utilizes a custom Faraday ring to stabilize the magnetic field regardless of coil excursion, voice coil frequency, or current. Driven by discrete Class-AB bi-amplification (25W woofer + 25W tweeter), the monitor preserves full musical dynamics across the spectrum.</p>\n\n      <h3>Key Technical Specifications:</h3>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Frequency Response (\xB13 dB):</strong> 60 Hz \u2013 35 kHz</li>\n        <li><strong>Maximum SPL:</strong> 102 dB SPL (peak @ 1 m)</li>\n        <li><strong>Woofer Amplifier:</strong> 25 W Class-AB RMS</li>\n        <li><strong>Tweeter Amplifier:</strong> 25 W Class-AB RMS (50 W Total RMS)</li>\n        <li><strong>Inputs:</strong> Balanced XLR (10 k\u03A9), Unbalanced RCA (10 k\u03A9 with sensitivity compensation)</li>\n        <li><strong>Acoustic EQ Settings:</strong> High-pass filter (Full / 80 Hz), Bass shelving (0\u2013250 Hz, \xB16 dB), Treble shelving (4.5\u201335 kHz, \xB13 dB)</li>\n        <li><strong>Cabinet:</strong> 12 mm MDF, genuine walnut veneer, black painted finish</li>\n        <li><strong>Mounting:</strong> Underside M6 inserts for K&M\xAE table/mic stands; Rear M6 inserts for wall/ceiling brackets</li>\n        <li><strong>Dimensions (H x W x D):</strong> 257 x 161 x 200 mm (10.1 x 6.3 x 7.9")</li>\n        <li><strong>Weight:</strong> 5.0 kg (11 lbs)</li>\n      </ul>\n    ',
