      "badge": '2.5-Way \xB7 Dual 5" Flax Cone \xB7 Double Passive Radiator',
      "sku": "FOCAL-SHAPE-TWIN",
      "description": '\n      <p>The <strong>Focal Shape Twin</strong> is the standard bearer and benchmark product of the Shape series. Featuring two passive radiators, woofers equipped with a new Flax sandwich cone, and the latest \u201CM\u201D-shaped Aluminium/Magnesium inverted dome tweeter, it is the perfect weapon of mass production for recording and mastering professionals.</p>\n\n      <p>Handcrafted in France, Shape Twin stands out through its extraordinary rendering over the entire audio spectrum, broad frequency response in the low end down to 40 Hz, and high SPL considering its compact dimensions. Its 2.5-way design provides a decisive acoustic advantage when controlling bass and lower mid-range registers\u2014the hardest to tame in small and medium rooms.</p>\n\n      <h3>Flax Sandwich Cones & TMD Surround</h3>\n      <p>The dual 5-inch woofers utilize Focal\u2019s patented <strong>Flax sandwich cone</strong> composed of high-quality French flax fibers encased in structural glass-fiber skins. One woofer reproduces frequencies from 40 Hz to 2.5 kHz while the second is dedicated to low-mid and sub-bass from 40 Hz to 250 Hz. Combined with <strong>TMD (Tuned Mass Damper) surround</strong>, it produces remarkable neutrality without masking effects.</p>\n\n      <h3>"M"-Shaped Inverted Dome Tweeter</h3>\n      <p>Focal\u2019s 1-inch aluminium-magnesium inverted dome tweeter features a distinctive <strong>\u201CM\u201D profile</strong> and a Poron\xAE suspension. This design achieves very low directivity for a flexible listening position, pristine high-definition detail up to 35 kHz, and fatigue-free mixing.</p>\n\n      <h3>Dual 8" Side-Firing Passive Radiators (Portless Design)</h3>\n      <p>Engineered without traditional bass reflex ports, Shape Twin utilizes <strong>dual 8-inch (20 cm) side-firing passive radiators</strong>. This allows the monitor to be positioned directly against back walls without boundary bass buildup or port noise.</p>\n\n      <h3>Neutral Inductance Circuit (N.I.C.) & Class-AB Tri-Amplification</h3>\n      <p>Focal\u2019s proprietary <strong>N.I.C. technology</strong> stabilizes the magnetic field regardless of driver excursion or current. Powered by discrete Class-AB tri-amplification (2x 85W woofers + 50W tweeter \u2014 210W total RMS), the monitor provides massive dynamic headroom and surgical precision.</p>\n\n      <h3>Key Technical Specifications:</h3>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Frequency Response (\xB13 dB):</strong> 40 Hz \u2013 35 kHz</li>\n        <li><strong>Maximum SPL:</strong> 110.5 dB SPL (peak @ 1 m)</li>\n        <li><strong>Woofer Amplification:</strong> 2 x 85 W Class-AB RMS</li>\n        <li><strong>Tweeter Amplification:</strong> 50 W Class-AB RMS (210 W Total RMS)</li>\n        <li><strong>Inputs:</strong> Balanced XLR (10 k\u03A9), Unbalanced RCA (10 k\u03A9 with sensitivity compensation)</li>\n        <li><strong>Acoustic EQ Settings:</strong> High-pass filter (Full / 45 / 60 / 90 Hz), Bass shelving (0\u2013250 Hz, \xB16 dB), Midrange EQ (160 Hz, Q=1, \xB13 dB), Treble shelving (4.5\u201335 kHz, \xB13 dB)</li>\n        <li><strong>Cabinet:</strong> 15 mm MDF, genuine walnut veneer, black painted finish</li>\n        <li><strong>Mounting:</strong> Underside M6 inserts for K&M\xAE table/mic stands; Rear M6 inserts for wall/ceiling brackets</li>\n        <li><strong>Dimensions (H x W x D):</strong> 478 x 211 x 279 mm (18.8 x 8.3 x 11.0")</li>\n        <li><strong>Weight:</strong> 11.0 kg (24.2 lbs)</li>\n      </ul>\n    ',
