      "description": "Ten Bands. Total Control.\nThe JOYO Band Controller is for bassists and guitarists who want real graphic-EQ precision on their board, not just a tone knob. With 10 dedicated faders from 31.25Hz to 16kHz, it's a strong fit for players correcting a boomy stage sound, cutting through a dense mix live, or switching between a 5-string bass and a 7-string guitar without losing coverage at either end. It also suits anyone who wants a visual, at-a-glance read on their EQ curve thanks to the LED on every band.\nJOYO Band Controller\nA true 10-band EQ pedal built for both bass and guitar, with a light-up fader for every band.\n\nThis 10-band EQ effect pedal is suitable for both bass and guitar, with a frequency range from 31.25Hz to 16kHz \u2014 covering 4-string and 5-string bass as well as 6-string and 7-string guitar. An independent Volume control sits on the pedal's right side, and the LED next to each fader flickers with the signal as you play.\n\n01\nEffect Type\n10-Band Equalizer\n02\nFrequency Range\n31.25Hz \u2013 16kHz\n03\nWorks With\nBass (4/5-string) & Guitar (6/7-string)\n04\nBypass\nTrue Bypass\n05\nPower\nDC 9V, 30mA\n06\nFootprint\n125 \xD7 78.5 \xD7 48 mm, 316 g\nWhy You'll Love It\n1\nTen Real Bands, Not Three\n31.25Hz, 62.5Hz, 125Hz, 250Hz, 500Hz, 1K, 2K, 4K, 8K, and 16K \u2014 each with its own dedicated fader. That's genuine graphic-EQ resolution in a pedal footprint, letting you notch out problem frequencies or shape a scooped or mid-forward tone with real precision.\n\nJOYO Band Controller 10 band faders labeled by frequency\n2\nBuilt for Bass and Guitar Alike\nThe 31.25Hz to 16kHz range is wide enough to cover 4-string and 5-string bass low end as well as 6-string and 7-string guitar top end \u2014 one pedal that moves between instruments without leaving frequencies uncovered.\n\nJOYO Band Controller input, DC 9V, and output jacks\nProcraft Insight\nEach fader's LED flickers with your signal, so you can see which bands are actually doing work while you play \u2014 useful for dialing in a live mix without staring down at knob positions.",
