      "sku": "AK-NORD-ELECTRO-7-61-KEY-STAGE-PIANO-MUG8GZOL",
      "description": "The much-anticipated Nord Electro 7 stage piano has arrived, and it lives up to expectations\u2014and then some. Each succeeding generation built on the acclaimed Electro bloodline, and its predecessors were all big sellers. The Electro 7 now lifts the performance standard even higher, with revised Piano, Organ, Synth, and Effects sections, real drawbars with LEDs, and a new color display, live mode, and push encoder for easy program selection.\n\n\n\nThe Electro 7 comes in three variants, featuring either 61 or 73 semi-weighted waterfall keys or a 73-note hammer-action keybed. Whatever you select, you\u2019ll be performing in style thanks to a sleek, lightweight, roadworthy chassis packed with excellent Nord sounds and effects. The Nord Electro 7 is suitable for live performance and sound creation, both onstage and in the studio, thanks to its extensive feature set.\n\n\n\nNord\u2019s famous organ section is onboard\n\nSince the creation of the company\u2019s first combination organ, Nord has prioritized superb sound design, effects manipulation, and playability. The Electro 7\u2019s organ section, based on the renowned Nord Organ 3, benefits from Nord\u2019s meticulous attention to detail while providing even more options for deep, authentic sound sculpting, including updated transistor organ models, Rotary Speaker emulation with selectable mic positions, and Slow/Fast and Stop controls. The Electro 7 has separate vibrato and chorus control over the upper and lower manuals, which is a must-have for the discriminating organist. Of course, having access to physical drawbars allows you to adjust your sound in real time.\n\n\n\nPowerful features provide the tools you need\n\nNord packed the Electro 7 with loads of features to make gigging and recording easier than ever. A new huge color display allows you to quickly examine your settings, effects, and more. You may also create splits and layers that mix the organ, piano, and sampling portions. The new Synth section has more settings for sample playback, analog and FM synthesis, mono and legato modes, glide and unison, a filter with resonance and FM partials, an ADR envelope for amp and filter, and synth vibrato.\n\n\n\nThe piano section now includes dynamic compression and unison settings. The Effects section has also been enhanced with controls for Ring Modulator, Rate/Amount, and Vibe, as well as a Compressor that can be selected globally or per section, a global Reverb with layer Send, and new amps, including the stunning Suitcase and Brit versions.\n\n\n\nThe Nord Electro 7 61-Key Stage Piano Features:\n\n Advanced stage piano featuring popular Nord Piano, organ, and synth sounds.\n Features 61 or 73 semi-weighted waterfall keys or 73-key hammer action.\n The organ part is based on the Nord Organ 3 with improved transistor organ models.\n New rotary speaker with adjustable mic placements and slow/fast/stop settings.\n Drawbar Live mode with settings for upper and lower manual.\n LED-enabled physical drawbars\n Improved piano part with dynamic compression and unison.\n The new synth section includes sample playback, analog and FM synthesis, mono/legato mode, glide and unison, filter with resonance and FM partials, ADR envelope for amp and filter, and synth vibrato.\n Improved Effects section with Rate and Amount, Ring Modulator, and Vibe settings.\n New amp models: Suitcase and Brit.\n Select a compressor by section or globally.\n Global reverb with per-layer send.\n Improved program section with new color display, Live Mode, and push encoder for easy program selection.\n Sleek, lightweight, and roadworthy chassis.\n Handcrafted in Sweden.",
