      "sku": "AK-NORD-ELECTRO-7-73-KEY-STAGE-PIANO-MUG8IU0S",
      "description": "The Nord Electro 7 enhances the Electro series with a powerful new Synth Section, dedicated per-section effects, and a revised panel design including a high-resolution color display. The Nord Electro 7 combines Nord\u2019s latest piano features with the organ and rotary speaker from the popular Nord Organ 3, providing extraordinary versatility in a lightweight, stage-ready instrument.\n\n\n\nThe Nord Electro 7 73 is a performance-oriented stage keyboard that builds on the Electro foundation with a 73-key semi-weighted waterfall action and a completely revamped sound engine. The Electro 7 73 is designed for musicians who want expressive organ performance, greater piano realism, and versatile synth capabilities. It provides hands-on control in a simplified, stage-ready configuration.\n\n\n\nNord\u2019s famous organ section is onboard.\n\nSince the creation of the company\u2019s first combination organ, Nord has prioritized superb sound design, effects manipulation, and playability. The Electro 7\u2019s organ section, based on the renowned Nord Organ 3, benefits from Nord\u2019s meticulous attention to detail while providing even more options for deep, authentic sound sculpting, including updated transistor organ models, Rotary Speaker emulation with selectable mic positions, and Slow/Fast and Stop controls. The Electro 7 has separate vibrato and chorus control over the upper and lower manuals, which is a must-have for the discriminating organist. Of course, having access to physical drawbars allows you to adjust your sound in real time.\n\n\n\nEngines for organs, pianos, and synthesizers\n\nThe Organ Section is based on the Nord Organ 3 engine and has a new rotary speaker with adjustable mic placements, slow/fast and stop options, and updated transistor organ models. Drawbar Live Mode allows for real-time performance management, with presets available for both upper and lower manuals, while actual drawbars with LED indications give instant visual feedback.\n\n\n\nThe revised Piano Section now includes Dynamic Compression and Unison for a more robust and present sound. A new Synth Section adds sample playback to the Electro 7, in addition to analog and FM synthesis. It has mono and legato modes, glide, unison, vibrato, ADR envelopes for amp and filter, and a filter with resonance and FM partials.\n\n\n\nProgram Control and Interface\n\nThe redesigned Program Section has a new color display and Live Mode, allowing for seamless program changes during performance. Push encoders are utilized throughout the instrument to choose programs, sounds, and categories, resulting in a standardized and fast workflow for both editing and live use.\n\n\n\nEffects and Amplification\n\nThe new Effects Section now features rate and quantity settings, ring modulation, and vibe effects. The Amp Section has a new Suitcase model and a new Brit amp, and compression may be adjusted per section or globally. A global reverb with configurable send per layer allows for versatile ambiance control across layered sounds.\n\n\n\nNord Electro 7 73-Key Stage Piano Features:\n\n Advanced stage piano featuring popular Nord Piano, organ, and synth sounds.\n Features 61 or 73 semi-weighted waterfall keys or 73-key hammer action.\n The organ part is based on the Nord Organ 3 with improved transistor organ models.\n New rotary speaker with adjustable mic placements and slow/fast/stop settings.\n Drawbar Live mode with settings for upper and lower manual.\n LED-enabled physical drawbars\n Improved piano part with dynamic compression and unison.\n The new synth section includes sample playback, analog and FM synthesis, mono/legato mode, glide and unison, filter with resonance and FM partials, ADR envelope for amp and filter, and synth vibrato.\n Improved Effects section with Rate and Amount, Ring Modulator, and Vibe settings.\n New amp models: Suitcase and Brit.\n Select a compressor by section or globally.\n Global reverb with per-layer send.\n Improved program section with new color display, Live Mode, and push encoder for easy program selection.\n Sleek, lightweight, and roadworthy chassis.\n Handcrafted in Sweden.",
