      "id": "novation-flkey-2-49-mug5z46l",
      "name": "Novation FLkey 2 - 49",
      "shortName": "Novation FLkey 2 - 49",
      "brand": "Novation",
      "category": "MIDI Controllers",
      "section": "pro-audio",
      "subcategory": "",
      "price": 32085,
      "originalPrice": 35e3,
      "stock": 10,
      "inStock": true,
      "isPreOrder": false,
      "stockStatus": "instock",
      "rating": 5,
      "reviewCount": 0,
      "badge": "",
      "sku": "AK-NOVATION-FLKEY-2-49-MUG5Z46L",
      "description": "Sketch beats and finish tracks fast with the keyboard controller for FL Studio. Four octaves of full-size, semi-weighted keys, polyphonic-aftertouch pads, and an array of knobs, faders, and buttons give you full control of your FL Studio projects. FLkey 49 is hardwired to your most important tools and workflows \u2014 from step sequencing in the Channel Rack to mixing, creating Patterns, and controlling plugins. \n\n\n\nThe only keyboard controller made for FL Studio \n\nPlay instruments, sequence Patterns, and take control of your mix: FLkey 49 gives you direct, hands-on access to the FL Studio tools and plugins you use most \u2014 from the Channel Rack and Step Sequencer to Sytrus, Harmor, and much more. \n\n\n\nCapture inspiration fast \n\nFLkey 49 features four full-sized octaves of great-feeling, semi-weighted keys plus pitch and mod wheels for added expression. And the built-in creative tools make melodies and chords simpler than ever: Avoid wrong notes with Scale mode, play full chords from a single key with Fixed Chord mode, and quickly create professional-sounding progressions from the pads using Chord Maps. The powerful arpeggiator makes it easy to create and mutate sequences that keep you inspired. \n\n\n\nLay down beats\n\nTrigger samples in the Channel Rack or sequence Patterns directly on the RGB pads. Prefer to play your beats in live? The 16 velocity-sensitive pads with polyphonic aftertouch are perfect for finger drumming with FPC, SliceX, and Fruity Slicer.\n\n\n\nFinetune and finish your tracks\n\nSet levels, sweep filters, dial in effects, navigate your Playlist, and more from eight endless encoders and nine precision faders. The crisp OLED display provides instant visual feedback about whatever you\u2019re adjusting. \n\n\n\nRefined and redesigned \n\nFLkey MK1 was the first MIDI keyboard controller made for FL Studio. Its successor makes it even easier to keep your creativity flowing with deeper connections to FL Studio\u2019s most important features plus semi-weighted keys, more expressive pads with polyphonic aftertouch, a crisp OLED display, and more powerful built-in creative tools. \n\n\n\nGo beyond FL Studio \n\nFLkey 49 works with your whole studio: Connect synths and other MIDI hardware via the full-size MIDI out port, take control of Novation Play and your NKS plugins, or craft custom control layouts for anything you like with Novation Components. Like to switch between FL Studio and another DAW? FLkey has you covered with Mackie HUI support. \n\n\n\nEverything you need to get started \n\nFLkey comes with a six-month trial of FL Studio Producer Edition, giving you everything you need to start creating right out the box. Need to brush up on your finger-drumming or keyboard skills? Explore a bespoke collection of lessons from Melodics. You also get Novation Play and a wide selection of premium instruments and effects from Native Instruments, Orchestral Tools, Klevgrand, and GForce.\n\n\n\n\nIncluded Software\n\nSix months of FL Studio Producer Edition\n\nKickstart your creativity with a six-month trial of the most popular FL Studio collection. The Producer Edition gives you everything you need to make music in any genre, including more than 100 individual instruments and effects, unlimited audio clips, stem separation, and a wide selection of loops, samples, and presets. \n\n\n\nMelodics\n\nMelodics is a unique desktop and mobile app that helps you learn to play the music that you love on keys or pads. Explore a bundle of bespoke lessons for Novation users, included free with FLkey.\n\n\n\nNovation Play\n\nThis exclusive collaboration with Klevgrand includes 80+ expertly designed basses, leads, pads, drum kits and more \u2014 all integrated seamlessly with FLkey\u2019s controls for an immediate, hardware-like workflow. \n\n\n\nGForce Bass Station\n\nBack in 1993, we introduced the world to a compact analogue synth with a colossal low end \u2014 the original Bass Station. Now, more than thirty years later, we\u2019ve partnered with analogue-modelling pioneers GForce Software to create the definitive virtual version of this cult classic. \n\n\n\nGForce Oberheim SEM\n\nThe Oberheim SEM emulates the classic Oberheim Synthesiser Expander Module, a powerful yet simple monophonic synth that delivers a massive punch, allowing you to craft incredible sounds instantly. \n\n\n\nGForce Oberheim OB-EZ\n\nA polyphonic synth with an iconic 80s sound, the Oberheim OB-EZ offers eight-voices of rich, captivating leads, basses, pads, and more. Use the Stereo Delay control to thicken your sound, add a spatial dimension, or apply lush reverb to achieve that signature Oberheim tone. \n\n\n\nGForce AXXESS\n\nThe Axxess synthesiser is ideal for crafting sounds across genres, from cinematic scores to hip-hop, offering extensive modulation options for diving deeper into sound design, along with an onboard sequencer for rhythmic patches. \n\n\n\nKlevgrand LUXE\n\nCompresses and saturate your sound in subtle-yet-musical ways with two selectable algorithms and a slider to set the desired strength. LUXE is an easy-to-use tool that simply makes your audio sound better. \n\n\n\nKlevgrand Slammer\n\nSlammer is a multi-sample drum plugin with 30 hard-hitting kits. Choose from a variety of natural and distorted drums, as well as percussive sounds, perfect for creating highly distinctive and instantly gratifying beats. \n\n\n\nOrchestral Tools Parallel Orchestra\n\nThis original spin on orchestral sampling pairs modern sound design with traditional acoustic instruments to add an unfamiliar twist to any track. Select from six individual expressive instruments spanning piano, strings, percussion, ambient textures and a full orchestral ensemble. \n\n\n\nNative Instruments Komplete Select\n\nChoose from three different bundles of essential production tools, each tailored to a specific style of production \u2014 Beats, Band, or Electronic. In each, you\u2019ll find a hand-picked selection of instruments and effects, including big names like Massive X, Battery, and iZotope Ozone Elements.\n\n\n\nWhat\u2019s In the Box\n\n\u2022	FLkey 2 49\n\n\u2022	1.5m USB type C-to-A cable",
